 And then they'll say, yeah, I'd rather locate my business here where the city also agrees it's a good place.

8624
06:32:58,660 --> 06:33:02,660
 I know I'm not going to have to find the city about it because it's already a place that they like.

8625
06:33:02,660 --> 06:33:09,660
 Then I'm going to choose that even if it's a little bit more expensive than going to this other site that might be less expensive.

8626
06:33:09,660 --> 06:33:22,660
 So you're looking for an overlay that can be applied to different commercial places rather than doing, putting that into an actual commercial zone so that we can be prescriptive about when this will benefit, where it's going to benefit.

8627
06:33:22,660 --> 06:33:31,660
 The idea that not every commercial area, there's going to be some commercial areas that probably deserve a little more scrutiny, right?

8628
06:33:31,660 --> 06:33:39,660
 That it might be a trickier situation and it should every time a business comes in, we may want to give that an extra look to make sure it's coming through.

8629
06:33:39,660 --> 06:33:45,660
 A perfect example is Ranches Crossing that's come out a few times trying to figure out how that works.

8630
06:33:45,660 --> 06:33:54,660
 Maybe that doesn't fall under something that makes sense for an artillery type overlay because it is in such a critical juncture of a state, right?

8631
06:33:54,660 --> 06:34:09,660
 But in other places that might need it, we need some sort of an oomph to kind of get it going or we want to push retail out into a certain spot.

8632
06:34:09,660 --> 06:34:12,660
 Do we need to do multiple ones?

8633
06:34:12,660 --> 06:34:24,660
 I'm just kind of thinking through this because when you have different categories of businesses, like if we're talking about retail food, that'd be a different thing than retail goods.

8634
06:34:24,660 --> 06:34:35,660
 Or if we're talking about distribution, are you thinking that there should be multiple, like, because you don't want to put it all into one, right?

8635
06:34:35,660 --> 06:34:40,660
 No, this would be specifically for retail because we already have the industrial RTI overlay.

8636
06:34:40,660 --> 06:34:43,660
 And my idea of this would be a retail approach.

8637
06:34:43,660 --> 06:34:47,660
 It would be more of a similar to how our RTI overlay works.

8638
06:34:47,660 --> 06:34:51,660
 There's a certain number or certain types of instances that are called out, right?

8639
06:34:51,660 --> 06:34:57,660
 So we only really give this to certain categories of businesses that would come into there.

8640
06:34:57,660 --> 06:34:58,660
 So we're not necessarily saying that.

8641
06:34:58,660 --> 06:35:04,660
 What I was thinking is the other ones we haven't talked about, like medical, like beautiful trauma,

8642
06:35:04,660 --> 06:35:13,660
 trying to attract the hospital to kind of moving the things out of their way to make that happen, or an educational something.

8643
06:35:13,660 --> 06:35:19,660
 Do we want to have something like that that really encourages that type of thing and move some of the roadblocks out of the way for them to say,

8644
06:35:19,660 --> 06:35:22,660
 "We're prepared for you to come here. Here's the steps that we've taken."

8645
06:35:22,660 --> 06:35:31,660
 Or do you think just to focus on the retail is kind of moving, and I'll defer to you or the council on the weather, I don't like this.

8646
06:35:31,660 --> 06:35:34,660
 What are the rest of you thinking?

8647
06:35:34,660 --> 06:35:39,660
 I personally think, I mean, I think his idea has some merit.

8648
06:35:39,660 --> 06:35:49,660
 If you look at what Bill Gaskell built right there on the corner, we really need to see every one of those side plants for every one of those drive-thru restaurants in my opinion.

8649
06:35:49,660 --> 06:35:53,660
 And I just think that you can open that up a little bit.

8650
06:35:53,660 --> 06:35:58,660
 If you have that prescribed within that area and you say, "These types of uses are going to be approved."

8651
06:35:58,660 --> 06:36:04,660
 As long as they meet whatever the minimum standards are, right, and get the staff the opportunity to do that, I'm not going to take issue with that.

8652
06:36:04,660 --> 06:36:12,660
 But I think where those are located is where I want to have some real contemplated discussion about where are we going to be able to do that.

8653
06:36:12,660 --> 06:36:16,660
 And, you know, how do you do it with some of the other uses?

8654
06:36:16,660 --> 06:36:18,660
 Rich, you're talking about medical and others.

8655
06:36:18,660 --> 06:36:21,660
 I mean, I think there are those zones, and that's not been a real issue.

8656
06:36:21,660 --> 06:36:26,660
 But in some of our commercial areas, we're getting a lot of dental offices and those types of things.

8657
06:36:26,660 --> 06:36:33,660
 Do we want to -- I mean, to his point, do you want to kind of separate that from where you are?

8658
06:36:33,660 --> 06:36:38,660
 We're going to get down a little bit where you can remove the professional offices from that type of use

8659
06:36:38,660 --> 06:36:43,660
 and congregate them perhaps in a little different area and make sure that the retail is front and center in some of those areas.

8660
06:36:43,660 --> 06:36:47,660
 I think that's something we can talk about.

8661
06:36:47,660 --> 06:36:51,660
 Because I hate to see all the best space being taken up by insurance agents and dentists.

8662
06:36:51,660 --> 06:36:54,660
 My son's a dentist, so.

8663
06:36:58,660 --> 06:37:05,660
 So, is there support then for moving to a liquor process or a --

8664
06:37:05,660 --> 06:37:11,660
 I think this is something about -- if this is okay, I could just work on some proposals for you and bring them to you

8665
06:37:11,660 --> 06:37:13,660
 and let me kind of steal over them at that point.

8666
06:37:13,660 --> 06:37:14,660
 Yeah.

8667
06:37:14,660 --> 06:37:15,660
 Yeah.

8668
06:37:15,660 --> 06:37:16,660
 Good idea.

8669
06:37:16,660 --> 06:37:17,660
 Okay.

8670
06:37:17,660 --> 06:37:21,660
 So, the next part of this is -- I call this industrial name recognition.

8671
06:37:21,660 --> 06:37:28,660
 So, establishing specific industries to pursue so that we're not just shotgun approaching everything with industrial.

8672
06:37:28,660 --> 06:37:34,660
 But then, we're planning and marketing sites with our property owners with a shared vision.

8673
06:37:34,660 --> 06:37:39,660
 And this extends also to everyone here in the room, council, mayor, everyone.

8674
06:37:39,660 --> 06:37:42,660
 We all understand these are the industries that we're pursuing.

8675
06:37:42,660 --> 06:37:48,660
 Every time you have conversations with anyone at the state, with the legislators, with any business people you have in mind

8676
06:37:48,660 --> 06:37:52,660
 or have relationships with, these are the industries that we're focusing on.

8677
06:37:52,660 --> 06:37:54,660
 This is why we believe we do good at them.

8678
06:37:54,660 --> 06:37:56,660
 This is where the land is that we have for them.

8679
06:37:56,660 --> 06:37:58,660
 These are the ways that we can make these work.

8680
06:37:58,660 --> 06:38:01,660
 This is the infrastructure that's going to make them work.

8681
06:38:01,660 --> 06:38:04,660
 This is the workforce where all of it's in, right?

8682
06:38:04,660 --> 06:38:09,660
 And then, marketing Eagle Mountain brand associated with these specific industries.

8683
06:38:09,660 --> 06:38:19,660
 So, working with Tyler in our own internal, you know, projects and whatnot, we're starting to associate the Eagle Mountain brand with these sorts of things as well.

8684
06:38:19,660 --> 06:38:25,660
 We start identifying with this industry, this industry, this industry, this is why, you know, going from there.

8685
06:38:25,660 --> 06:38:32,660
 So, and I'll explain, well, I'll provide some recommendations on what those industries could be.

8686
06:38:32,660 --> 06:38:34,660
 But I'd like your feedback on that.

8687
06:38:34,660 --> 06:38:38,660
 So, the last one is what I call data mastery.

8688
06:38:38,660 --> 06:38:42,660
 So, investing in a couple of data collection tools or one data collection tool.

8689
06:38:42,660 --> 06:38:48,660
 And really where this comes from is kind of linked to this before.

8690
06:38:48,660 --> 06:38:54,660
 There's, it depends on the company, but a lot of companies now, especially the bigger national ones,

8691
06:38:54,660 --> 06:39:01,660
 they have their own proprietary data systems or some will rely on other various data sources.

8692
06:39:01,660 --> 06:39:09,660
 And when you present your own data as a city to them, they sort of disregard it.

8693
06:39:09,660 --> 06:39:17,660
 Because they feel like what power does a city have to really tell us what they actually know about the market or the trade area, whatever it is.

8694
06:39:17,660 --> 06:39:24,660
 They look to third party sources more than they do direct sources unfortunately.

8695
06:39:24,660 --> 06:39:29,660
 So, I've done a lot of work to provide a lot of good data that has been really helpful.

8696
06:39:29,660 --> 06:39:38,660
 I've gotten feedback over the past several months from a lot of people who have been very pleased to see the data and how it's been packaged and brought to all these different people.

8697
06:39:38,660 --> 06:39:43,660
 I think it's made a lot of impact, but it's not taking us quite over the edge with some of them.

8698
06:39:43,660 --> 06:39:48,660
 An example of this is I've had lots of conversations with Lowe's in particular.

8699
06:39:48,660 --> 06:39:57,660
 And they say, PeopleMountain seems great, what they're showing us is great, but when we run things for our own models or when we consult this other source,

8700
06:39:57,660 --> 06:40:01,660
 we now have a bit of a disagreement between the different data sources.

8701
06:40:01,660 --> 06:40:04,660
 We need a third party to help us go over that hurdle.

8702
06:40:04,660 --> 06:40:10,660
 But beyond that, our own data sources are somewhat limited in that we only really say so much.

8703
06:40:10,660 --> 06:40:15,660
 We can say we have this population, but we can't say where is that population going?

8704
06:40:15,660 --> 06:40:17,660
 Where is that population shopping?

8705
06:40:17,660 --> 06:40:19,660
 How are they shopping?

8706
06:40:19,660 --> 06:40:20,660
 Where are they working?

8707
06:40:20,660 --> 06:40:22,660
 All these sorts of different things.

8708
06:40:22,660 --> 06:40:27,660
 But the fact that we do over a thousand building permits a year, that's going to be lumber.

8709
06:40:27,660 --> 06:40:36,660
 That means we're going to have a thousand washers, a thousand dryers, a thousand refrigerators, all part of that business model in the contractor section,

8710
06:40:36,660 --> 06:40:38,660
 which should be a huge win for somebody.

8711
06:40:38,660 --> 06:40:43,660
 I can't believe nobody is jumping on the fact that we're still building more than anybody else.

8712
06:40:43,660 --> 06:40:46,660
 And that's the thing that's really frustrating about it.

8713
06:40:46,660 --> 06:40:51,660
 I'll tell them all about that sort of stuff, but they don't input that into their own models.

8714
06:40:51,660 --> 06:40:52,660
 They're still looking at them.

8715
06:40:52,660 --> 06:40:54,660
 They're very rigid and data driven.

8716
06:40:54,660 --> 06:40:56,660
 And this is how things have evolved over time.

8717
06:40:56,660 --> 06:40:58,660
 It's extremely data driven now, right?

8718
06:40:58,660 --> 06:41:07,660
 And so what I'm trying to get to is to try and get not to just their level as far as delivering data, but try and get ahead of them now.

8719
06:41:07,660 --> 06:41:12,660
 Try and get where we're saying, I know you have your data, but my data is better.

8720
06:41:12,660 --> 06:41:16,660
 And I have more of it that tells a much better story than yours can.

8721
06:41:16,660 --> 06:41:19,660
 And we want them to be in awe of what they're seeing.

8722
06:41:19,660 --> 06:41:23,660
 It's going to be basically a slam dunk every time they see our data.

8723
06:41:23,660 --> 06:41:25,660
 And there are tools out there that get us there.

8724
06:41:25,660 --> 06:41:29,660
 Obviously, it takes an investment to get access to that.

8725
06:41:29,660 --> 06:41:32,660
 So something like Buxton.

8726
06:41:32,660 --> 06:41:47,660
 So a little bit of a side note, but somewhat tied into that last one.

8727
06:41:47,660 --> 06:41:53,660
 What kind of, you know, who are we targeting and what are we doing to target them and whatnot?

8728
06:41:53,660 --> 06:42:00,660
 I had a citizen Tuesday night after mayor's Wednesday, I guess, after that RDA discussion.

8729
06:42:00,660 --> 06:42:02,660
 Why are we even doing a tax break?

8730
06:42:02,660 --> 06:42:04,660
 I was told by a previous council member.

8731
06:42:04,660 --> 06:42:06,660
 You may know who it was.

8732
06:42:06,660 --> 06:42:07,660
 It might have been Colby.

8733
06:42:07,660 --> 06:42:12,660
 I mean, that it's one of a kind, right?

8734
06:42:12,660 --> 06:42:21,660
 We're going to do one RDA or one TIF per kind of industry, meaning one data center, one Tyson food.

8735
06:42:21,660 --> 06:42:23,660
 That's used to be how we did it.

8736
06:42:23,660 --> 06:42:26,660
 Well, I don't think we've ever done that because there's a history of the things.

8737
06:42:26,660 --> 06:42:29,660
 That's used to the model that he wanted to do, right?

8738
06:42:29,660 --> 06:42:30,660
 Yeah.

8739
06:42:30,660 --> 06:42:35,660
 And so the citizens are saying, well, why are we doing another RDA for the same type of businesses?

8740
06:42:35,660 --> 06:42:38,660
 Well, I think the model is not one of a kind.

8741
06:42:38,660 --> 06:42:41,660
 It's more of a deescalating.

8742
06:42:41,660 --> 06:42:45,660
 If you come again and you're not the first guy, then it's going to be a lot less.

8743
06:42:45,660 --> 06:42:46,660
 Yeah.

8744
06:42:46,660 --> 06:42:50,660
 Now that's the case in data centers because they don't fit in the same box as a normal RDA.

8745
06:42:50,660 --> 06:42:51,660
 It's not commercial.

8746
06:42:51,660 --> 06:42:52,660
 Their values are so high.

8747
06:42:52,660 --> 06:42:55,660
 The taxes are, they have to, right?

8748
06:42:55,660 --> 06:42:59,660
 My question is, is how are you courting these guys?

8749
06:42:59,660 --> 06:43:04,660
 And are we offering some kind of TIFs at what rate?

8750
06:43:04,660 --> 06:43:10,660
 I personally, not necessarily in favor of TIFs for commercial and retail type businesses,

8751
06:43:10,660 --> 06:43:15,660
 but are we just taking them golfing them to lunch or you're going to those meetings?

8752
06:43:15,660 --> 06:43:18,660
 Are we like, why would they come to Eagle Mountain?

8753
06:43:18,660 --> 06:43:22,660
 Any of these guys besides data centers, which we're obviously good at.

8754
06:43:22,660 --> 06:43:26,660
 I tell you, I think he hits the nail on the head with number two where you have the industrial name recognition.

8755
06:43:26,660 --> 06:43:31,660
 Because from my perspective, I think it comes back down to what our Eagle Mountain brand is.

8756
06:43:31,660 --> 06:43:41,660
 And I think that it's natural to court and to bring a bicycle manufacturer here or an ATV manufacturing facility.

8757
06:43:41,660 --> 06:43:48,660
 Some services, some industries that will service that, perhaps equestrian facilities of some sort.

8758
06:43:48,660 --> 06:43:56,660
 All of that, maybe it's a North Face gear production facility that makes outdoor gear.

8759
06:43:56,660 --> 06:44:04,660
 But I think those are the types of businesses that we're going to automatically be advertising for through our branding efforts.

8760
06:44:04,660 --> 06:44:12,660
 And I think there's a natural fit there where there can be a symbiotic relationship of the city maintaining our brand,

8761
06:44:12,660 --> 06:44:17,660
 according to those manufacturers to our city that support that brand,

8762
06:44:17,660 --> 06:44:24,660
 and working in a tandem to support their products and their growth,

8763
06:44:24,660 --> 06:44:28,660
 and also to help recognize what our brand is.

8764
06:44:28,660 --> 06:44:35,660
 Well, I think part of the comment, too, to help Evan to get to an RTI or to a REI or type,

8765
06:44:35,660 --> 06:44:39,660
 you know, some kind of that kind of business, even the outdoor recreation and whatnot,

8766
06:44:39,660 --> 06:44:45,660
 is although I'm against it, of course, the state now says on retail what we can do with tips anyway,

8767
06:44:45,660 --> 06:44:48,660
 but are we, can we help with infrastructure needs?

8768
06:44:48,660 --> 06:44:52,660
 And can we, I think that's going to be the key to bringing these people in here.

8769
06:44:52,660 --> 06:44:56,660
 And in the meantime, I don't know that as a council, at least we haven't given direction,

8770
06:44:56,660 --> 06:45:00,660
 and I don't know that we're using that tool.

8771
06:45:00,660 --> 06:45:05,660
 It goes back to the, there was a conversation a little bit before.

8772
06:45:05,660 --> 06:45:12,660
 There's an objective under the strategic goals or an action about developing a business policy.

8773
06:45:12,660 --> 06:45:19,660
 And so that policy would be trying to determine what is appropriate based on one of these businesses range,

8774
06:45:19,660 --> 06:45:24,660
 but that obviously the policy would come through the city council to kind of get your, I guess, blessing,

8775
06:45:24,660 --> 06:45:26,660
 as far as what does that look like so that we're all the same.

8776
06:45:26,660 --> 06:45:28,660
 Well, I think that's the conversation I'm talking about.

8777
06:45:28,660 --> 06:45:29,660
 What are we interested in?

8778
06:45:29,660 --> 06:45:34,660
 Maybe we should consider some reduced fees of some sort to court, something like that.

8779
06:45:34,660 --> 06:45:36,660
 You know, where you're charging and impact fee.

8780
06:45:36,660 --> 06:45:39,660
 Maybe we should say, look, we really want your industry here.

8781
06:45:39,660 --> 06:45:41,660
 You align well with our vision.

8782
06:45:41,660 --> 06:45:44,660
 You're a participant in our brand.

8783
06:45:44,660 --> 06:45:48,660
 And we'd like to have you be known as part of the Eagle Mountain.

8784
06:45:48,660 --> 06:45:50,660
 Well, I think that's what I'm interested in that.

8785
06:45:50,660 --> 06:45:52,660
 So I think we ought to have those discussions.

8786
06:45:52,660 --> 06:45:55,660
 And if those are some tools you're looking for, let's have that discussion.

8787
06:45:55,660 --> 06:45:57,660
 What does that look like?

8788
06:45:57,660 --> 06:46:02,660
 But do you think the discount on fees is going to make a big difference?

8789
06:46:02,660 --> 06:46:03,660
 I think the RTI.

8790
06:46:03,660 --> 06:46:04,660
 That's not who it is.

8791
06:46:04,660 --> 06:46:05,660
 Might make the difference.

8792
06:46:05,660 --> 06:46:11,660
 So I think the RTI did as well as it did for us because it was a clear landing path.

8793
06:46:11,660 --> 06:46:21,660
 Because that's worth more than thousands of dollars in discounts and fees to them because of the site selection.

8794
06:46:21,660 --> 06:46:27,660
 So that's just, I mean, it's a tool, but I don't know that it's going to be one that brings them in.

8795
06:46:27,660 --> 06:46:32,660
 But maybe it needs to be an Eagle Mountain brand overlay.

8796
06:46:32,660 --> 06:46:33,660
 Maybe that's what it needs to be.

8797
06:46:33,660 --> 06:46:39,660
 And if you fit in our brand, then you're going to have a leg up on your competition and going through the approval process.

8798
06:46:39,660 --> 06:46:41,660
 Whatever that looks like.

8799
06:46:41,660 --> 06:46:44,660
 So like with the preference for like outdoor type companies?

8800
06:46:44,660 --> 06:46:45,660
 Absolutely.

8801
06:46:45,660 --> 06:46:46,660
 I would want to do that.

8802
06:46:46,660 --> 06:46:53,660
 If we could get a Columbia, a North Face, if we could get a Calisocchi to come build them or even those that are selling them or Honda.

8803
06:46:53,660 --> 06:46:56,660
 I think those things align really well with our brands.

8804
06:46:56,660 --> 06:47:00,660
 Or I'm not a mountain biker, but Steve, what's a nice mountain bike?

8805
06:47:00,660 --> 06:47:01,660
 A Cannondale.

8806
06:47:01,660 --> 06:47:02,660
 I don't know, a Cannondale.

8807
06:47:02,660 --> 06:47:04,660
 There's a ton of great brands, yeah.

8808
06:47:04,660 --> 06:47:05,660
 Okay.

8809
06:47:05,660 --> 06:47:16,660
 But so even if we, even if we reached out to a manufacturer of high-end mountain bikes, wouldn't that just want us to have that in our city?

8810
06:47:16,660 --> 06:47:26,660
 Well, and honestly, some of it might just be the fact that they'll be paying less taxes because of the cost of land and all that here.

8811
06:47:26,660 --> 06:47:27,660
 Yeah.

8812
06:47:27,660 --> 06:47:36,660
 And we'll talk more about this as we talk about kind of some marketing industries, but you know, that definitely could be something to pursue.

8813
06:47:36,660 --> 06:47:37,660
 I do like that.

8814
06:47:37,660 --> 06:47:38,660
 Yeah.

8815
06:47:38,660 --> 06:47:39,660
 Yeah.

8816
06:47:39,660 --> 06:47:40,660
 You can find brand overlay.

8817
06:47:40,660 --> 06:47:41,660
 That's pretty cool.

8818
06:47:41,660 --> 06:47:42,660
 Yeah.

8819
06:47:42,660 --> 06:47:43,660
 It's tried and true.

8820
06:47:43,660 --> 06:47:44,660
 Yeah.

8821
06:47:44,660 --> 06:47:50,660
 If you come help and support our brand, we're going to make it easy for you because you're the type of, you're the type of big business or small business.

8822
06:47:50,660 --> 06:47:51,660
 That'll be one of us.

8823
06:47:51,660 --> 06:47:52,660
 You want.

8824
06:47:52,660 --> 06:47:58,660
 To also answer kind of more of a customer grace and questions earlier, we do kind of take two different approaches.

8825
06:47:58,660 --> 06:48:14,660
 We're trying to do that more now where, you know, obviously, as we try and get our name out there, recognized for certain things about outdoor recreation, about whatever it is, you know, we do whatever we can to kind of create our name out there so it doesn't come to us.

8826
06:48:14,660 --> 06:48:16,660
 But we don't want to just wait for that, obviously.

8827
06:48:16,660 --> 06:48:18,660
 We want to do something that's more proactive.

8828
06:48:18,660 --> 06:48:21,660
 And so we've already been doing some of that already.

8829
06:48:21,660 --> 06:48:25,660
